To create a responsive grid layout with CSS Grid, you’ll define a grid area using `display: grid` on a container, then use fractional units (`fr`) and `repeat()` functions to let columns resize smoothly across devices.

### Basic Example

```html
<div class="grid-container">
  <div class="card">1</div>
  <div class="card">2</div>
  <div class="card">3</div>
  <div class="card">4</div>
  <div class="card">5</div>
  <div class="card">6</div>
</div>
```

```css
.grid-container {
  display: grid;
  /* Default: 3 equal columns */
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  /* Optional: gap between items */
  gap: 1rem;
}

.card {
  background: #f0f0f0;
  padding: 1rem;
  min-height: 100px;
}
```

This creates 3 equal columns that fill the available space.

### Making It Responsive

Use media queries to change the number of columns on smaller screens:

```css
/* Large screens */
.grid-container {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
}

/* Tablets */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .grid-container {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }
}

/* Mobile */
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .grid-container {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
```

### Advanced: Auto-Fit Columns

Instead of a fixed number of columns, you can let the grid automatically fit as many as possible:

```css
.grid-container {
  display: grid;
  /* Auto-fit: as many columns as fit, minimum 250px wide */
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
}
```

This single rule is often enough to be responsive on its own:
- On small screens → fewer columns (maybe 1)
- On medium screens → 2 columns
- On large screens → 3+ columns

### Grid Areas (Optional)

If you need specific placement:

```css
.grid-container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  grid-template-areas:
    "header header header"
    "sidebar main main"
    "footer footer footer";
}

.header    { grid-area: header; }
.sidebar   { grid-area: sidebar; }
.main      { grid-area: main; }
.footer    { grid-area: footer; }
```

### Tips

- Use `fr` for flexible, proportional columns.
- Use `repeat()` to define many columns concisely.
- Use `auto-fit` + `minmax()` for automatic responsiveness without many media queries.
- Always set a gap to control spacing between grid items.

